Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Fix deferred ACN determinants produced by referenced types

An ACN determinant may be declared inside a referenced type while controlling
a sibling field outside that type. Closure conversion handled determinants
consumed by referenced types, but not determinants produced by them. With
--acn-v2, the generated C therefore referred to an undeclared local instead of
passing the determinant across the reference boundary.

Expose such producer determinants as deferred ACN parameters and patch them in
the scope that owns the dependent field. Honor initializers attached to C
backend locals, which carry the deferred state, and accept the explicit
one-bit Boolean encodings that use the same representation as BOOL1.

Add a focused regression in a separate acn-v2 test directory. It generates,
strictly compiles, and runs a Boolean determinant produced by one referenced
child and consumed by an optional sibling.

